OL,3,GNEWSA'Mischief Night' name legitimises
OL,4,Acrime, leaders say
OL,5,
OL,6,FTwo Merseyside councillors have said
OL,7,Freferring to the night before Halloween
OL,8,F"Mischief night" legitimises crime.
OL,10,FThey spoke after a number of incidents
OL,11,Fon 30 October, including one in which a
OL,12,Fbaby was injured when a brick was
OL,13,Fhurled at a bus, and one in Huyton in
OL,14,Fwhich 20 youths were filmed vandalising
OL,15,Fcars.
OL,17,FKnowsley Green councillor Chantelle
OL,18,FLunt said: "We need to stop calling
OL,19,Fthis mischief night. It's criminal
OL,20,Fdamage. It's harming communities".
OL,23,APub: 05-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
